/-!
# GAGA consequences and uniformisation for the Jacobian logarithm

Auxiliary results for the logarithmic coordinates on the analytic Picard group of a smooth
projective curve over `ℂ` (`MMP.Conductor.exists_isZLattice_exponential_of_isProjective`).

For a projective scheme `C` over `ℂ`, GAGA identifies `H¹(C^an, 𝒪)` with the algebraic `H¹`,
compatibly with multiplication by constants, so it is finite dimensional; the analytification of
a projective integral scheme with a `ℂ`-point is connected. A uniformisation of a compact group by
`ℂⁿ` has a full lattice as kernel, and a local exponential, obtained from a local logarithm by the
inverse function theorem in étale charts, extends to such a uniformisation. Finally, the three
library models of the Picard group of a ringed site are compared.

## Main results

* `MMP.JacobianLogarithm.lattice_of_uniformisation`: the kernel of a uniformisation of a compact
  group by `ℂⁿ` is a discrete full lattice.
* `MMP.JacobianLogarithm.exists_uniformisation_of_localExp`: a local exponential extends to a
  uniformisation.
* `MMP.JacobianLogarithm.exists_localExp_of_localLog`: local exponential coordinates from a local
  logarithm.

## References

* [P. Griffiths, J. Harris, *Principles of Algebraic Geometry*][griffithsharris1978], Ch. 2 §6.
-/

@[expose] public section

